=== CLARIFICATION: Day 1 and Day 100 Valuations ===
Timestamp: Code review and improvement

USER QUESTION:
- Will day 1 and day 100 valuations always exist for all assets?

INVESTIGATION:
✅ Verified all 15 assets have complete data:
   - Each asset has valuations for all 100 days
   - Day 1 valuations exist for all assets
   - Day 100 valuations exist for all assets

KEY INSIGHT:
The data includes "theoretical" valuations even before an asset's available_on_day.
Example: asset_14 is available on day 50, but has valuations for days 1-49 as well.

This is a DATA DESIGN CHOICE that enables:
- Standardized comparison across all assets
- Fair ranking regardless of availability date
- Consistent baseline for performance measurement

IMPROVEMENTS MADE:
1. Added explicit comments explaining why we use day 1 & 100
2. Added warning messages for missing data (defensive programming)
3. Added tests to verify data completeness:
   - test_all_assets_have_day_1_valuations
   - test_all_assets_have_day_100_valuations
   - test_all_assets_have_complete_valuations
4. Updated strategy-analysis.md with data assumptions section

CODE CHANGES:
- src/strategies/buy_and_hold_strategy.py: Added comments and warnings
- test/test_services/test_data_loader.py: Added 3 new validation tests
- docs/strategy-analysis.md: Added "Data Assumptions" section

ASSUMPTION DOCUMENTED:
"All assets have valuations for days 1-100, even if not available until later.
This allows standardized performance comparison across all assets."

RISK MITIGATION:
- Tests will catch if future data doesn't meet this assumption
- Warning messages will alert if data is incomplete
- Code gracefully skips assets with missing data

